# The chapter skip, RIGHT half: it receives no input at all. Every position it takes here comes from
# the left half's single long press.
#
# It must heal rather than step. A skip is not a number of turns, so an implementation that replayed
# it as steps would either land short or walk the whole chapter -- and the heal it takes must be to
# the sender's page plus its own role offset, which is what puts it one page ahead on the spread.
log pageflip-skip-right: start
expect_timeout 90000
expect Entering activity: Home
wait 800
tap confirm
expect Entering activity: EpubReader
expect PageFlip link up as right
expect peer present
wait 8000
screenshot /screenshots/pf-sk-right-00.bmp
# Driven entirely by the other device's long press. The line carries the SENDER's landing, and this
# device seeks there and takes one further step for its role.
expect PageFlip heal
wait 10000
screenshot /screenshots/pf-sk-right-01.bmp
wait 1500
log pageflip-skip-right: done
quit
